{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835688-request-for-advice-playing-future-covers","id":835688,"title":"Request for advice: playing future Covers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-23T05:35:02-08:00","id":835688,"title":"Request for advice: playing future Covers","content":"Hi. I would like to propose a game to my gaming group. I would not tell them the name of the game. They would play normal individuals, that are slowly losing the battle against various threats, and find themselves in a position to accept soul pacts, without necessarily understanding what that entails. Then, little by little, demons would replace the poor guys/gals and help the process along for the other members of the circle. (I would take the player apart and brief him.)<br /> Depending on the actions of the players, I envision two outcomes: either they go full demons or they manage to pay their debts and solve their problems without losing themselves in the process.<br /> That is the rough idea. I am looking for advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/634-marmaduke","name":"marmaduke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T06:50:43-08:00","id":835722,"title":"","content":"There isn't a correlation between a cover and a demon beyond the facade they represent. Once the mortals are assimilated, if you let them play the demons cashing in, they become different characters altogether.<br /> <br /> That is, per RAW. Maybe those specific individuals were part of some esoteric Infrastructure. Maybe something of them lingers in the demons, or /and angels. Maybe they fell before being summoned by a matrix. <br /> <br /> Let us know how you spin it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T07:01:54-08:00","id":835730,"title":"","content":"Exactly. I would take the player apart and tell him &quot;Your old character doesn't exist anymore. Once [event from the contract] happened, the salesman/seductress/politician you signed the providential contract with was able to incorporate your whole existence to his own. Let's talk about your new demon character, wearing your old character as a Cover in a game of techgnostic espionage. Don't tell the other players at the table. Your objective is now to help your demon buddies achieve the contractual conditions required to complete their own soul pacts. Functionally, you are now an enemy of the other player characters. By the way, the clock is ticking for your demon buddies as their old Cover is very brittle.&quot;<br /> That is the basic idea. Looks like a way to introduce the players to a life of paranoia. I am looking for ideas on the way to proceed, like the general setup of the game. The context would be demons trying to infiltrate some place they think is valuable. A government agency? A government? A megacorporation?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/634-marmaduke","name":"marmaduke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T08:01:37-08:00","id":835782,"title":"","content":"Something that may put a stick on your wheel is that all terms of the contract must be spelled out, and IIRC, it won't work if they don't know what it entails.<br /> <br /> Demons usually sign outright Soul Pacts by playing on sheer desperation. A deal with the devil to have my daughter's life restored, for example (there's an Exploit for that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T11:21:23-08:00","id":835892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835688-request-for-advice-playing-future-covers?p=835782#post835782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that may put a stick on your wheel is that all terms of the contract must be spelled out, and IIRC, it won't work if they don't know what it entails.<br /> <br /> Demons usually sign outright Soul Pacts by playing on sheer desperation. A deal with the devil to have my daughter's life restored, for example (there's an Exploit for that).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, all the terms have to be <i>listed</i>, but the signer doesn't have to actually <i>read</i> them. It's completely stupid for something of this magnitude, but also completely in-character for quite a few people.<br /> <br /> Demons also like to bury their terms and conditions in dense legalese. It has to be possible to understand it, but that doesn't factor people turning their brains off after being confronted with a 40 page EULA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T11:30:31-08:00","id":835896,"title":"","content":"Could be fun to procure a real life, boring to hell business contract, change names, insert soul pact clause, and propose it as a prop to the player?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/634-marmaduke","name":"marmaduke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T14:13:31-08:00","id":836019,"title":"","content":"Someone actually posted the in-character contract (or a link to it) that their player posed to a person. Hilarious.<br /> <br /> I'm in favor of listing them whenever possible. Makes for great notes, as well as a chance to engage in subtle humor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T15:49:10-08:00","id":836069,"title":"","content":"Do remember, during Soul Pact negotiation, demons loose their ability to lie, except by misdirection and omission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T20:18:29-08:00","id":836196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835688-request-for-advice-playing-future-covers?p=836069#post836069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do remember, during Soul Pact negotiation, demons loose their ability to lie, except by misdirection and omission.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think the inability to lie in writing in the particular context of pactwork would be less of a concern than the whole &quot;sign in blood&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T00:21:11-08:00","id":836283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835688-request-for-advice-playing-future-covers?p=836069#post836069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do remember, during Soul Pact negotiation, demons loose their ability to lie, except by misdirection and omission.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that the terms of the written contract must be true, not that the demon is unable to lie. I can tell you you're signing in blood for xyz, but if you don't read the contract and see that you're really getting abc, tough luck.<br /> <br /> Is that not the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T00:53:24-08:00","id":836287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835688-request-for-advice-playing-future-covers?p=836019#post836019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone actually posted the in-character contract (or a link to it) that their player posed to a person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would love the link.<br /> Question: is it necessary for the signatory to understand the language the contract is written with?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835688-request-for-advice-playing-future-covers?p=836196#post836196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think the inability to lie in writing in the particular context of pactwork would be less of a concern than the whole &quot;sign in blood&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question: does the signatory have to know that the ink in the pen the demon hands him contains a bit of his own blood?<br /> <br /> Perhaps it would be easier to entice player characters to sign if the contract is proposed in the context of a roleplaying game? (Like, the players characters could be teenagers playing the game of Devil: The Tumble... or something more sophisticated.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/634-marmaduke","name":"marmaduke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T04:53:25-08:00","id":836347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835688-request-for-advice-playing-future-covers?p=836196#post836196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would think the inability to lie in writing in the particular context of pactwork would be less of a concern than the whole &quot;sign in blood&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right! I forgot that key, little detail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T07:36:58-08:00","id":836395,"title":"","content":"Bah, it's only blood. Maybe the charming gent in the suit is only being theatrical?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T08:28:12-08:00","id":836421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marmaduke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835688-request-for-advice-playing-future-covers?p=836287#post836287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would love the link.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only have the copy I made of it, unfortunately, not the original (for credit). Here's a link to the copy: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1pr1s5RWa_X6TWi3KETMZPKglF3fX1AqAoi03hTI1sww/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T16:24:08-08:00","id":836733,"title":"","content":"A good laugh, thanks for the link!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/634-marmaduke","name":"marmaduke","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T17:23:43-08:00","id":838875,"title":"","content":"Looking at the rules for a pact a demon flat out can't lie though wording things evasively or in a misleading manner are fair. The problem comes in that you also can't obscure the terms of the actual terms. I'm not a hundred percent sure what that last part means though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T18:02:56-08:00","id":838887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/835688-request-for-advice-playing-future-covers?p=838875#post838875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the rules for a pact a demon flat out can't lie though wording things evasively or in a misleading manner are fair. The problem comes in that you also can't obscure the terms of the actual terms. I'm not a hundred percent sure what that last part means though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It means the fundamentals of the bargain have to be understood and you can't just walk around the town square with a clipboard full of form letters for people to sign under the pretense of it being a petition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Pacts can be informal affairs, a simple declaration of \u201cYou (the mortal) gain X if I (the demon) gain Y.\u201d</b> They can also be highly formal, full of legalese and fine print, employed by demons looking to bind unwary humans. Most are somewhere in between, though many demons try to slip in loopholes and misleading ambiguity, enough to benefit them but not leave the mortal any wiggle room. Poorly worded pacts do just that; more than one epic tale has describes a mortal\u2019s quest to excise himself from a contract with a demon. <b>Ultimately, a pact is simply an exchange of some kind: the mortal agrees to give up something to the demon and the demon provides a service in turn.</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A contract must always be signed willingly by a human\u2019s own hand, but this does not preclude coercion. Any form of influence or direct intimidation (i.e., \u201cSign this or I will kill you\u201d) is allowed, as long as the mortal signs the contract herself. Using mind-control powers to force an assignee\u2019s hand voids any deal made. <b>The mortal doesn\u2019t need to know what exactly it is she is signing. If she fails to read the fine print, it\u2019s on her head. Clever demons use this to their advantage, although as much as they lie, the person in question still must know the terms of the deal.</b> Misdirection and manipulation are both common tactics in making pacts. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T07:17:07-08:00","id":839142,"title":"","content":"The question is: wouldn't the requirement to know the terms of the contract void the capacity to be misleading on them? Or merely being present in the text preclude it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T09:31:10-08:00","id":839250,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on interpretation. But one read is that the signer must know they are giving <i>something</i> up, but they might not know the full implications of what they are agreeing to, or understand <i>exactly</i> what they are giving up fully.<br /> <br /> Say you trade someone your friend. The signer might think the Demon owns the friend, can now be the friend's friend, etc. They don't need to understand that they've traded away the contextual historical role of &quot;X's Friend&quot; to the Demon.<br /> <br /> Or even the classic Soul Pact. If you are a diligent student of the occult, you might know that Souls are exchangeable, and don't contain the intellect/memory/mind of a person, so trading yours away is costly, but reversible. But that's not what the Demon means by Soul Pact...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-29-2016, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}